      en: ["The second-largest power station in Israel by generation capacity.", "Named after Pinhas Rutenberg, the founder of the Israel Electric Corporation.", "Located on the coastline just north of the city of Ashkelon.", "Its primary chimneys stand at a height of approximately 250 meters.", "Features a deep-water pier designed to handle large coal-carrying vessels.", "Plays a critical role in providing power to the southern districts and the Negev."],
